  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - Commencement of development (Full Permission) - The development to which this permission relates shall be commenced not later than the expiration of 3 years from the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 2 - Approved Plans - The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans: [insert plans]",
    "Condition : 3 - Materials as Specified - The facing materials to be used for the development hereby permitted shall be those specified in the application form unless otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority.",
    "Condition : 4 - Landscaping  (Implementation) - All hard and soft landscape works shall be carried out in accordance with the approved details as shown on Proposed Site Plan. The works shall be carried out in the first available planting season following the completion of the development or prior to the occupation of any part of the development, whichever is the sooner, and any trees which die within a period of 5 years from the completion of the development, are removed or become seriously damaged or diseased or are dying, shall\nbe replaced in the next planting season with others of same approved specification, unless the Local Planning Authority gives written consent to any variation. All hard surfacing and means of enclosure shall be completed before the development is first occupied.",
    "Condition : 5 - Refuse & Recycling (Implementation) - The development hereby approved shall not be occupied until the refuse and recycling storage facilities shown on the approved plans have been fully implemented and made available for use. These facilities shall thereafter be retained for use at all times.",
    "Condition : 6 - Cycle Parking to be implemented - The development hereby permitted shall not be occupied until the cycle parking shown on the plans hereby approved has been provided and made available for use. These facilities shall be retained for the occupants of and visitors to the development at all times.",
    "Condition : 7 - Sustainability (Water Consumption) - No part of the development hereby approved shall be occupied until evidence has been submitted to, and approved in writing by, the Local Planning Authority confirming that the development has achieved internal water consumption rates of no greater than 105 litres per person per day \n\nReason: To ensure that the development achieves a high standard of sustainability and makes efficient use of resources and to comply with the following Development Plan policies for Merton: Policy SI 2 and SI 3 of the London Plan 2021 and Policy CS15 of Merton's Core Planning Strategy 2011.",
    "Condition : 8 - Following a site visit from the case officer, it appears that some works had already commenced, and these are not in accordance with the approved plans. \n\nThe decision hereby assessed and approved is solely based on a proposed development to convert the property into 2 flats as shown on the submitted drawings (see condition 2 for list of approved plans). The applicant is also reminded that planning condition 7 (sustainability) is a pre-occupation condition. \n\nGiven the site condition of the site as evidenced by the case officer, this matter has been referred to planning enforcement to monitor for compliance and a failure to accord with the approved details can lead to formal enforcement action."
  ],
